Make the GStreamer audio sink media.role overridable via WEBKIT_GST_MEDIA_ROLE.

SFOS routes the system media volume (the hardware volume keys, via
module-meego-mainvolume) only to PulseAudio streams whose media.role is in its
route table — "x-maemo" on Sailfish (/etc/pulse/x-maemo-route.table). WebKit
hardcodes media.role to "video"/"music" on its audio sinks
(MediaPlayerPrivateGStreamer::createAudioSink -> createPlatformAudioSink ->
createAutoAudioSink, which stamps it onto the pulsesink stream-properties here),
and neither role is in that table, so the volume keys cannot attenuate browser
audio at all — the root cause behind all the el.volume / MainVolume2-poll hacks.

This can't be fixed from the environment: PULSE_PROP[_OVERRIDE] only sets the
client/context proplist, and an explicit per-stream media.role (which WebKit
sets) wins — device-verified. So override the role at the point WebKit sets it.

createAutoAudioSink is the single chokepoint in the default config (the audio
mixer / webkitAudioSinkNew path is off unless WEBKIT_GST_ENABLE_AUDIO_MIXER),
covering HTML5 <audio>/<video>, the mixer device sink, and speech. With
WEBKIT_GST_MEDIA_ROLE=x-maemo (set in deploy/runtime-common.sh) every browser
audio stream lands in the system media-volume group = native, browser-level
volume. Unset = upstream behaviour. Device-proven: an x-maemo stream tracks the
volume step (29%@2 -> 95%@10) while "music"/"video" stay put.
--- a/Source/WebCore/platform/graphics/gstreamer/GStreamerCommon.cpp
+++ b/Source/WebCore/platform/graphics/gstreamer/GStreamerCommon.cpp
@@ -1164,6 +1164,16 @@
 
 GstElement* /* (transfer floating) */ createAutoAudioSink(const String& role)
 {
+    // SFOS: route browser audio into the system media-volume group. The Nemo
+    // mainvolume policy (module-meego-mainvolume, driven by the hardware volume
+    // keys) only steps streams whose media.role is in its route table — "x-maemo"
+    // on Sailfish. WebKit's default "video"/"music" roles are ignored by it, so
+    // the volume keys cannot attenuate browser audio. WEBKIT_GST_MEDIA_ROLE forces
+    // a single media.role onto every audio sink. Unset = upstream behaviour.
+    String effectiveRole = role;
+    if (const char* envRole = std::getenv("WEBKIT_GST_MEDIA_ROLE"); envRole && *envRole)
+        effectiveRole = String::fromUTF8(envRole);
+
     auto* audioSink = makeGStreamerElement("autoaudiosink"_s);
     g_signal_connect_data(audioSink, "child-added", G_CALLBACK(+[](GstChildProxy*, GObject* object, gchar*, gpointer userData) {
         auto* role = reinterpret_cast<StringImpl*>(userData);
@@ -1179,7 +1189,7 @@
             auto& clientName = getApplicationName();
             g_object_set(object, "client-name", clientName.ascii().data(), nullptr);
         }
-    }), role.isolatedCopy().releaseImpl().leakRef(), static_cast<GClosureNotify>([](gpointer userData, GClosure*) {
+    }), effectiveRole.isolatedCopy().releaseImpl().leakRef(), static_cast<GClosureNotify>([](gpointer userData, GClosure*) {
         if (auto* roleImpl = reinterpret_cast<StringImpl*>(userData))
             roleImpl->deref();
     }), static_cast<GConnectFlags>(0));
